{
  "id": "Compound::DB00155 - Gene::11240",
  "verbalization": "L-citrulline is implicated in the regulation of Protein-arginine Deiminase Activity through its interaction with multiple Padi proteins, including Padi1, Padi3, and Padi6. These proteins participate in the same biological process, which is central to the deamination of arginine residues. The shared involvement of these Padi proteins in the same pathway suggests a coordinated functional relationship, possibly mediated by common regulatory mechanisms or structural interactions. The high scores in all three paths indicate a strong, consistent link between L-citrulline and Padi2, as it is directly linked to the same activity through different Padi proteins. This suggests that L-citrulline may influence the activity of Padi2 through a shared pathway, potentially by modulating the activity of its interacting Padi proteins. The integration of these paths highlights a mechanism where L-citrulline exerts its effect through a network of Padi proteins, ultimately influencing the activity of Padi2.",
